{"_meta":{"openai/toolInvocation/invoked":"Choose a mix","openai/toolInvocation/invoking":"Setting up your week\u2026","openai/widgetAccessible":true,"securitySchemes":[{"type":"noauth"},{"scopes":["openid","email","profile","offline_access"],"type":"oauth2"}],"ui":{"visibility":["app","model"]}},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":false,"title":"Choose a protein mix"},"description":"Compatibility planning entry point for older callers. create_weekly_menu is the main planner. Returns optional weekly planning configuration as data: the user picks a protein mix (a balanced default is offered, such as 2 chicken, 1 fish and 1 veg for four dinners) and people per dinner, for building the week. The chooser has no priority setting; a priority the user states (quick, healthy, comfort) is passed as the priority parameter. Provides optional mix configuration when the user wants to choose the structure before recipe generation. The default mix is a suggestion shown to the user, not a choice made for them. Returns configuration only: no recipes are chosen and no account is needed; for a signed-in account, its diet (vegetarian, vegan, pescatarian) shapes the mixes offered. When the request already states a counted mix, slotRequirements, a mixPreset or 'surprise me', this tool builds the draft directly, exactly as create_weekly_menu does. Takes the same parameters as create_weekly_menu.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"brief":{"description":"Free-text brief, e.g. 'quick midweek family dinners, no fish'.","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"configurationId":{"description":"Set by the weekly chooser widget: the chooser this week is built from, so the widget can find it again after a reload.","pattern":"^configure_[0-9a-f-]{36}$","type":"string"},"dietary":{"items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"dinnersCount":{"description":"H